                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1603-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ></span>Telefunken Elektroakustik Ela M 80 SH</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Cardioid Dynamic Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The M80SH is a shortened body version of the popular M80 model. The shorter body and built-in mic clip allows for easier placement around a tight drum kit.</p><p>The mic has a fixed Cardioid polar pattern. Its frequency response is somewhat flat from 200Hz&ndash;2000Hz, with a broad presence peak (+8dB) from 2500Hz&ndash;13kHz. Response below 200H; and above 13kHz falls off sharply.</p><p>The M80-SH ships with Chrome and Black head grills, leather bag and five meter SGMC-5 right-angle XLR cable.<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Telefunken-USA/M80SH">Telefunken Elektroakustik Ela M 80 SH</a> is also known as: M80SH, M80 SH.</p><p>The mic was released in 2013.</p>
